# Four half-fed turbines, and they beat two full ones.
#
# Two exchangers make 200 steam a tick and a turbine takes 80, so a plant with
# two turbines throws forty away every tick and never notices. Four turbines at
# fifty each take all of it: 132 MW against `03-compact`'s 108, for four more
# components and half as much utilisation per machine.
#
# Which of those two is the better answer is exactly the argument the brief
# refuses to settle, and the reason there is no single score. What experiment
# 08 adds is that the trade is now visible: a hall of four small machines does
# not look like a plant with two big ones, and nobody had to label either.

machine "Turbine Hall"
brief power

reactor   R1  at 0,0   throttle 50

exchanger HX1 at 5,0
exchanger HX2 at 5,4

turbine   T1  at 9,0
turbine   T2  at 9,3
turbine   T3  at 9,6
turbine   T4  at 9,9

generator G1  at 13,0
generator G2  at 13,3
generator G3  at 13,6
generator G4  at 13,9

pump      W1  at 0,5

wire R1.heat -> HX1.heat
wire R1.heat -> HX2.heat
wire W1.water -> HX1.water
wire W1.water -> HX2.water

wire HX1.steam -> T1.steam
wire HX1.steam -> T2.steam
wire HX2.steam -> T3.steam
wire HX2.steam -> T4.steam

wire T1.rotary -> G1.rotary
wire T2.rotary -> G2.rotary
wire T3.rotary -> G3.rotary
wire T4.rotary -> G4.rotary
